-- title:
--   Affine chart at a supersingular place, full level, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, and $M' \ge 1$ is a natural number with $q \nmid M'$. A rigidity guard is imposed on the auxiliary level: a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ is fixed.
--
--   **Base valuation and supersingular places.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Here `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the $\kappa$-subfield of the Laurent series field $\kappa((Q))$ generated by `jqModC κ` (the $j$-expansion $Q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$ over $\kappa$) and its $M'$-fold rescaling `jqNModC κ M'`. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is given, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places: those places $w$ (a place being a valuation subring of the function field containing $\kappa$, proper and with principal ideals) which are rational, i.e. $\kappa$ surjects onto the residue field of $w$, which satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`. One such place $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   **The two modular function fields and the constant reduction.** `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` is the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathbb Q((Q))$ generated by the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d$ of $M'$, and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is its coefficientwise base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, namely the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ generated by the image of that field under `coeffEmb`. The field `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 M') (levelH q M')`, the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ to the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, together with a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, subject to the structure's axioms: an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ iff its image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$; the residue map is compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants; every non-zero element of the big field can be scaled by a constant into the integers with non-zero residue; $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees; and orders of functions are carried to orders by pushing divisors forward along $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element whose image lies in $A$. The hypotheses on the pullback $A \cap k_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ ℚ̄)` are: it is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), and its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`). The hypothesis `hκ` says that $A = (A \cap k_0) + \mathfrak m_A$ in the following sense: for every $a \in A$ there is $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and uniformiser data.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (so $K_b = k_0$), $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those whose image lies in $A$, and $\varpi_b$ is a non-zero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equip `fieldBar q M'` with the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Then there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (i) The compositum of the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and of $F_0$ is everything: `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap ℚ̄ (fieldBar q M'))) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`.
--
--   (ii) For $x \in k_0$: the image of $x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (iii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (iv) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (v) Residual transcendence: there is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p \in k_0[X]$ all of whose coefficients have image in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then for every $n$ the image in $F_0$ of the $n$-th coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (vi) Passage through $s$: let $g \in \mathbb Q((Q))$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` and suppose its coefficientwise image, as an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$. Assume furthermore that $g$ is regular wherever $j$ is, in the sense that for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$; and assume that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$. Then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$, and as an element of $F_0$ it lies in $W_0$; moreover, for every $c \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between that image of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (vii) Level stability: for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — the automorphism singled out by the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, and the identity if no such automorphism exists — maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ the element $f$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if its image under this automorphism, viewed in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (viii) Linear disjointness over every finite layer: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ which is finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of the image of $K'$ and $F_0$: if the family $c$ is linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in `fieldBar q M'`, then every $a_i$ vanishes.
--
--   (ix) The affine chart: there exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that
--
--   (a) for $a \in A_b$ the image of $a$ in $B$, viewed in `fieldBar q M'`, is the image of $a \in K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of the image of $K_b$ and $F_0$;
--
--   (c) every element $f$ of that compositum satisfies $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (d) $B$ is formally smooth over $A_b$ and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (e) the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and, as such, in $W_0$;
--
--   (g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element;
--
--   (h) $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation: $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$;
--
--   (i) the image in `fieldBar q M'`, under `hle`, of the base change of `jq` lies in $B$;
--
--   (j) for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $B$ into $B$;
--
--   (k) identification of the special fibre with a Drinfeld curve: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (with $\mathbb F_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`), given that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) — the fixed field inside $\operatorname{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the actions `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$ — such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s`, that is `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` (for $q = 2$ the numerator is $12$ if that value of $j$ is $0$ and $1$ otherwise); the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; for $a \in A_b$, $\rho$ of the image of $a$ in $B$ is the image in the Drinfeld quotient field of the residue in $\kappa$ of $a$ viewed in $A$; every element $z$ of the quotient field satisfies $z\,\rho(h) = \rho(g)$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$; an element $z$ of the quotient field lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if, viewed in [`DrinfeldCurve.drinfeldFunctionField q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L12), it lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and, finally, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that the pair consisting of the reduction `redQ q γ` in $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $1 \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\gamma,u)\mapsto \det(\gamma)\,u^{q+1}$), and every $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, the value of $\rho$ at that element, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, equals the image of $\rho(f)$ under `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` applied to that pair.
--
--   This is the case $q = 2$, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the construction of the supersingular part of a semistable model of the full-level modular curve over small constants: it produces simultaneously the descended field $F_0$ with its discrete valuation ring $W_0$ attached to the supersingular place $s$, and an affine chart $B$ over the base discrete valuation ring $A_b$ whose fibre modulo $\varpi_b$ is identified, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level action, with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve of level $q$ in characteristic $q$. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd), where the local stalks of the resulting model are analysed.
